**How to implement.** Putting a kit item into a slot of the table, as a semantic message (001 §P `AssignSlot`; 001 §J 'each holding an item or nothing'; the S8.2 brief: 'Placing an element binds a slot … Messages CreateSetup, AssignSlot and SwapSlot are pure updates with tests'). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: (1) On the model extension holding `itemModelCaption` (step 241): `member model.tryItemModelChoice (item : Item) : ItemModelChoice option`, the model as the window's stores resolve it: a `PresetInstance (modelVersion, id)` whose `model.library.tryGetEntry id` answers a `SourceItem` or a `PolarizerItem` is its `SourcePresetChoice` or `PolarizerPresetChoice`; a `SampleInstance (modelVersion, v)` whose `model.samples.resolveVersion v` answers a sample is `StackSampleChoice (sampleModel, v, sample)`; an `ItemModelVersionInstance v` whose `model.itemModels.resolveItemModelVersion v` answers a version is its `LibraryModelChoice` (step 216); anything else, `None` or an error, is `None`. `itemModelCaption` becomes the resolved choice's `caption` (step 241) or `(model not in the library)`, its three store reads replaced by this one resolution, so its texts are unchanged. (2) `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `AssignSlot of Library.ElementId * ItemId option`, with a one-line doc: put a kit item, or nothing, into that slot of the table. (3) Its arm writes nothing, so a read-only kit takes it too. A slot id the table lacks sets `kitStatus` to `Not assigned — <describe>` of `UnknownSetupSlotErr` naming it. `None` makes the slot `withoutItem` (step 258). `Some id` takes the item of that id in `kitItems` (else `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming the id) and its `tryItemModelChoice` (else `UnknownSlotItemErr` naming the item's label and that its model is not in the library), and the slot becomes `slot.withItem item choice` (step 258); a refusal sets `kitStatus` to `Not assigned — <e.describe>` and changes nothing else; on success the slot is replaced in `elements` and `kitStatus` is `None`. The setup records the slot at the next CreateSetup, SaveSetup or commit (steps 260-262). No other message, field or option is added. Tests, in `SetupModelTests` (step 260), whose kit holds items added through `AddItem` (step 239): `LP1` (the `PresetIds.polarizerLp` preset, `FixedMounting`), `QZ` (the glass plate at version 1), `Laser` (the HeNe preset) and `LPd` (that polarizer preset, `DialMounted DialNegative`, its `dialZero` set to 10° through `SetParameterState`, step 240). `AssignSlot puts a kit item into a table slot bound to its library entry, and AssignSlot of nothing empties it`: with a linear polarizer and a sample added, `AssignSlot (polarizer, Some LP1)` holds `ItemInSlot (LP1, PlacementTurn)` bound to the preset, `AssignSlot (sample, Some QZ)` binds the glass plate with its supported emission, and `AssignSlot (polarizer, None)` holds `EmptySlotContent` with the binding kept; no kit file changes. `AssignSlot of an item that does not fit the slot, that the kit lacks, or whose model the library lacks is told and changes nothing` : `Laser` into the polarizer slot sets a `kitStatus` starting `Not assigned` and naming `Laser`; an id the kit lacks, a slot id the table lacks, and a test-local item put in `kitItems` whose sample version the store lacks each do so too, and `elements` are unchanged. `a dial-mounted item is recorded with its reading and drawn through its current zero`: `LPd` assigned to the polarizer at R1 30° and `CreateSetup` of `Dial` write a `DialTurn` of −20° (10° − 30°); after `LPd`'s `dialZero` is set to 20°, `ActivateSetup (SetupName "Dial")` draws the polarizer at R1 40°, within 1e-12. `ItemsPanelModelTests` and `ItemsPanelTests`' facts on the model caption pass unchanged. All choice construction and matching in this step MUST use step 216's payloads, including the resolved ItemModelVersion for source, ideal-polarizer and stack choices. Fixtures MUST obtain those versions from step 210's shipped model entries; runtime resolution MUST use the stored version through ItemModelProxy, never manufacture a model or use a preset/sample as the model. Existing parameter values and optical results MUST be preserved. tryItemModelChoice MUST first resolve modelVersion for every instance and validate its form. Only then MAY it resolve the preset/sample dependency and construct the choice with that model version. An unresolved model MUST return None even when the preset/sample resolves. The slot assignment tests MUST exercise this refusal and a successful snapshot-only reopen.

**Acceptance.** After AssignSlot lands, `model.tryItemModelChoice` MUST resolve an item's model through the window's stores, `itemModelCaption` MUST read it, and `AssignSlot` MUST put a fitting kit item into a table slot bound to its library entry, empty a slot, and refuse an item that does not fit or is unavailable, writing nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `AssignSlot puts a kit item into a table slot bound to its library entry, and AssignSlot of nothing empties it`, `AssignSlot of an item that does not fit the slot, that the kit lacks, or whose model the library lacks is told and changes nothing` and `a dial-mounted item is recorded with its reading and drawn through its current zero`, the count rising by 3; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.
